@@ -9,3 +9,9 @@ other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards
 - `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` — JSON Pointer evaluation (RFC 6901). Returns the value the pointer
   refers to; throws `JsonPointerError` if the pointer is invalid or does not resolve (missing member,
   out-of-range index, `-`, or descending into a scalar). Does not modify the document.
+- `applyPatch(document, patch)` — JSON Patch (RFC 6902) with the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`,
+  `move`, `copy` and `test`. Returns the patched document as a new value; neither the document nor the patch
+  is modified, and the patch is atomic (on failure nothing is returned). Throws `JsonPatchError` if the patch
+  is invalid or an operation fails (missing target, out-of-range index, failed `test`, `move` into its own
+  child). Paths follow RFC 6901, including `-` for appending to an array. Choices where the RFC is silent:
+  removing the document root is rejected, and `__proto__` is just an ordinary member name (no prototype effect).
